  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-61658\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>The polyhedron is a <strong>pentagonal prism</strong> since it has two identical pentagonal faces connected by equal parallel line segments.</p>\n<p>Also, notice that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The solid is not a pyramid since a pyramid must have triangular faces (except, possibly, for the base) that meet at a single point.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles. Due to the same reasons, the solid is not a cube.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\">Rectangular prism</div></div>",
